WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY
---------------------
This repository was previously dual-licensed: MIT for the code, all rights
reserved for the `skills/` directory. It is now MIT throughout, including the
skill templates, their meta-prompts and their manifests.

The reason is simple: the code was already MIT, so the service was already
free to clone. Holding three templates back protected nothing real, while it
did slow down the circulation that makes the work useful.

